{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 5.6 with 20% lactic acid or HCl. Fresh yeast extract is prepared by autoclaving a 20% suspension of commercial baker's yeast in distilled water for 30 minutes at 121\u00b0C, allowing the suspension to settle overnight at 2 to 8\u00b0C, decanting and further clarifying the supernatant by centrifugation. The extract prepared in this manner contains 1.5% solids and if not to be used within a few days, should be frozen or freeze-dried immediately."
                    }

{
                        "step": "After sterilization, aseptically add 1 ml/l of a 10% solution of acetylacetone in ethanol."
                    }

